<details><summary>Reveal the full containment argument</summary>
If a sequence vanishes for every index $k\ge n$, it also vanishes for every $k\ge n+1$, so $S_n\subseteq S_{n+1}$. The vector $e_n$ is zero after index $n$ but nonzero at index $n$, hence it lies in $S_{n+1}\setminus S_n$. Because $S_0=\{0\}$, the intersection of the ascending chain is its first rung.
