Every multiple of $2^{n+1}$ is a multiple of $2^n$, so $D_{n+1}\subseteq D_n$. The constant function $2^n$ belongs to $D_n$ but not $D_{n+1}$. Thus the chain descends strictly. See also [ideal filtrations](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filtration_(mathematics)).
