Finite-variable polynomial rings over fields are Noetherian by [Hilbert's basis theorem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilbert%27s_basis_theorem), so they have no infinite ascending ideal staircase. Their [Krull dimension](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krull_dimension) can nevertheless be positive because dimension concerns finite chains of prime ideals. The two measurements answer different questions.
